processTerminalMethod(selector, arguments) -> result or signal
    Validate terminal launch, exact text input, integral byte offset and terminal size arguments.
    Dispatch launching, input, draining text, recent output, cursor-based output and resizing.
processStartTerminal(program, arguments, directory, columns, rows)
    Start a child with controlling terminal and inherited session configuration.
    Retain a nonblocking master terminal. Capture output concurrently and reap child independently.
    Report launch or setup errors in completed Process state; preserve final child output before completion.
    If descendants keep the terminal open after the child exits, allow one second to drain before closing it.
appendTerminalOutput(state, bytes)
    Retain at most one MiB of recent output and one MiB of unread output, counting total and dropped unread bytes.
    Also feed ordinary Process capture buffers with their existing bounded-first-output semantics.
terminalReadFrom(state, byteOffset) -> JSON TerminalReadResponse
    Reject future offsets. Clamp stale offsets to the oldest retained byte and report skipped byte count.
    Return at most 64 KiB as base64, preserving arbitrary bytes and split Unicode characters.
    Return the offset immediately after the supplied bytes, oldest retained offset, current status and nullable exit code.
    Never consume output belonging to another reader. Each viewer maintains its own next offset.
